ard 13 years and a nine Episode  television series is currently in  production and if all goes according to  plan it'll be released sometime early in  2021 the Tom Clancy verse is no stranger  to its source material being used in  both video games and Hollywood with the  recent success of the Jack Ryan series  on Amazon it looks like paramount is  also looking to get in on the action by  producing two movies focus  on the character of John Clarke Michael  B Jordan will be playing the character  in two movies one based on the novel of  Rainbow six and the other based on its  origin story without remorse  Stefano's Salima the director behind  Sicario day of the soldato has also been  attached to direct the Resident Evil  movie franchise is proof that success  and longevity can be found in video game  movie adaptations after numerous well  performing movies yes we know they  weren't actually all that good but they  did do very well at the box office  Capcom survival horror franchise is now  shuffling onto Netflix in the form of a  series details are few and far between  currently but the show will reportedly  expand upon the game's lore and deepen  the mythology of the expanded Resident  Evil universe this series is currently  gearing up for pre-production this  spring with actual production following  suit a little later in the year speaking  of Resident Evil Paul WS Anderson the  man behind the movie franchise is  bringing another beloved Capcom property  to the big screen this time it's Monster  Hunter the movie will be led by the  Resident Evil movie franchises leading  lady Milla Jovovich complete with an  ensemble cast made up of Ron Perlman  Tony yaw Megan good and Ti Sony is  currently aiming for an early September  2020 release which hopefully also means  we'll start seeing a steady stream of  trailers for the monster flick in the  very near future Dante the gun slinging  sword wielding silver haired devil  hunter is coming to Netflix The Devil  May Cry Netflix series will be developed  by Adi Shankar executive producer of the  highly successful and very well-received  animated Castlevania series that's also  streaming on Netflix in a recent  interview Shankar revealed that he even  acquired the rights to work on the  series himself so that in his words the  jabronis in Hollywood don't this one up  as well I think it goes without saying  that he plans on playing this animated  series very close to the chest and he's  clearly very passionate about it given  that he and his team knocked the  Castlevania series out of the park  that's pretty encouraging even after  hitting a couple of early production  bumps the Minecraft adaptation is still  set to hit theaters in March of 2022  with Nick and Norah's Infinite Playlist  director peter sollett in charge of the  movie now this isn't the first time  minecraft dipped its blocks into the  narrative space with  he'll tell games creating a very  successful episodic series back in 2017  and while we're not exactly sure how  closely the movies gonna resemble the  game itself we can imagine it's gonna be  very very blocky in terms of plot  details the games developer mo yang said  that it follows the story of a teenage  girl and an unlikely group of  adventurers and they need to save the  beautiful blocky over world after the  malevolent ended dragon tries to destroy  it all produced by Aquaman and fast and  furious 7 director James Wan the Mortal  Kombat reboot is currently in production  in Australia with theatrical release set  for March 2021 with its casting being  officially announced the movie is  looking to be a nice mix of seasoned  actors and fresh faces for one to  destroy with some brutal combat and yes  let's combat with a que aside from that  little is known about the upcoming  Mortal Kombat movie but with a producer  like James Wan involved I think it's  pretty safe to say that this upcoming  version will be nothing short of an  action-packed blockbuster that's right  if you haven't heard already the  mustachioed Italian plumber is leaping  into the big screen once again but this  time he's gonna be appearing in an  animated feature and whether you were  too young to remember or simply just  chose to mentally block out the 1993  movie entirely here's a nice little  reminder of why Mario being animated  this time around is probably a good idea  [Music]  yeah those word goombas these guys we're  supposed to be these guys oh and yeah  this is what Yoshi looked like yikes  this time around however Nintendo will  no doubt do more to make sure their  precious plumber is treated right given  how popular and lucrative the Mario  franchise is now if Sega can make it  work for Sonic surely Nintendo can do  the same for the Mario Bros and there  you have it those are some upcoming  video game adaptations that we're  weirdly excited for are there any games  not in production that you think deserve  the Hollywood treatment let us know in  the comments section down below and for  more on all the games movies and TV  shows we listed make sure to keep your  eyes peeled to GameSpot  you
 

